  Descent: ['The gradient is the uphill direction. Descent steps against it, with $\\eta$ setting how far.', 'Drag the start, then raise $\\eta$ until the path zig-zags. Increase $\\kappa$ and see the limit tighten.'],
  Convexity: ['A convex curve lies under all of its chords, which guarantees that any local minimum is the global one.', 'On the bumpy shape, drag the chord ends to find a violation. Then move the start point and see where descent lands.'],
  GaussianArea: ['For a continuous variable, probability is the area under the density. Height alone means nothing.', 'Use the ±σ buttons to see the standard percentages, then shrink $\\sigma$ until the peak passes one.'],
  BayesDensity: ['Each class has a density and a prior. Their weighted ratio is the posterior.', 'Drag the means apart, then change the prior and note which way the decision point moves.'],
  DotProduct: ['The dot product multiplies matching entries and adds. Its sign says whether two arrows agree.', 'Drag $v$ around $u$ and find where the value is zero. Watch the green shadow change sign.'],
  ShapeDrill: ['For $AB$, columns of $A$ must equal rows of $B$. The result has rows of $A$ and columns of $B$.', 'Write the two shapes side by side, compare the inner pair, and read the outer pair. Type the shape like 3x4.'],
  DerivativeDrill: ['The power rule gives the slope of each term of a polynomial separately.', 'Differentiate each term, then substitute the given $x$. Do it on paper before you check.'],
  VarianceDrill: ['Variance measures spread as the average squared distance from the mean.', 'Compute the mean, subtract it from each value, square, and average.'],
